# Jira — creating Test issues

Edit the table for your instance.

| What | Value |
|------|--------|
| **Project key** | `EPMRPP` |
| **Issue type** | `Test` |
| **Label** (mark AI-generated Tests) | `ai-generated` |
| **Test Steps** field (preconditions + steps) | `customfield_19206` |
| **Expected result** field | `customfield_19207` |

Use these when creating or updating **Test** issues (e.g. in `jira_createIssue` / `jira_updateIssue` payloads). **Every** new Test must include the **`ai-generated`** label (e.g. `labels` inside `customFields` when the tool expects it). Ensure that label exists in Jira or can be added on create, per your project settings.

**Before creating Tests:** Resolve **which issue is the story** (**`STORY_KEY`**). A dispatch or pasted **Sub-task** is not the story—**link** each new Test to the **story** and put **`STORY_KEY`** in **summaries**, never the Sub-task key when they differ. Details: **`.cursor/rules/ai-test-generator.mdc`** (**Always use STORY_KEY — verify first**).
